  lex_splices_err_stray_eof.pcpp - Lexical: a backslash ending the file

  Break step of lex_splices: a splice is a backslash before a newline,
  so one that ends the file with no newline after it is a stray
  character, LX0004. The marked line ends in that backslash, so its
  marker is a block-comment marker.
  Its bytes are part of the test (see above): edit it with an editor
  that keeps them as they are.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_splices_err_stray_eof;

/*
  @@test
    kind error
  @@end
*/

begin
  println("{}", 1);
/* // ERROR LX0004@33 // */ end.\